@{
  Layout = "_Layout";
}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>About Us</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/lib/bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" />
  <link rel="stylesheet"
    href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/bootstrap-icons/1.10.0/font/bootstrap-icons.min.css" />
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=MedievalSharp&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    html,
    body {
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      height: 100vh;
      background: url('../images/BackgroundForest.jpg') no-repeat center center fixed;
      background-size: cover;
      font-family: 'MedievalSharp', cursive;
    }

    .formCard {
      backdrop-filter: blur(6px);
      background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4);
      border-radius: 20px;
      color: white;
      width: 95%;
      max-width: 1000px;
      padding: 2rem;
      box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.37);
      margin: auto;
      margin-bottom: 5%;
      margin-top: 5%;
    }

    .About-Us-h1 {
      font-size: 3rem;
      text-align: center;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }

    .About-Us-txt p {
      font-size: 1.1rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
    }
  </style>
</head>

<body>
  <section style="padding-top: 5%;">
    <div class="formCard">
      <h1 class="About-Us-h1">About Us</h1>

      <div class="About-Us-txt">
        <p>OnLit began and was founded on a shared interest in books. Our passion for reading brought together a team of
          individuals who understood the value and impact of a well-told story.</p>

        <p>Being avid readers ourselves, we recognized the limitations of many existing digital reading platforms. We
          wanted to create an experience that felt as intimate and flexible as reading a physical book, while also
          embracing the advantages of technology.</p>

        <p>To achieve this, we prioritized personalization features that let users tailor their reading environment—from
          font styles and sizes to background colors and reading modes. Our goal was to give readers the freedom to
          customize their experience to fit their unique preferences.</p>

        <p>We also placed a strong emphasis on accessibility, ensuring that OnLit could be used by people with a wide
          range of needs. This includes support for screen readers, text-to-speech functionality, and other assistive
          technologies that make reading more inclusive.</p>

        <p>Finally, we integrated communicative features that bring a social element to reading. Whether it’s sharing
          notes, discussing chapters, or joining book clubs, OnLit makes it easier to connect with others over the
          stories you love.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</body>

</html>
